          "summary": "Combining mean-field theory and random matrix theory, the authors link correlation propagation to the Neural Tangent Kernel in the limit of infinitely wide and infinitely deep networks. They show that propagation to infinite depth is possible only at a single critical point, where the NTK becomes proportional to the output correlation, and validate the predictions on finite-width, finite-depth networks.",
